{{also|extrêmophile}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|extreme|-o-|-phile}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|ecology}} An [[organism]] that [[live]]s under [[extreme]] [[condition]]s of [[temperature]], [[salinity]] etc; commercially important as a [[source]] of [[enzyme]]s that operate under similar conditions.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=w:Bill Bryson|title=A Short History of Nearly Everything|publisher=BCA|page=207
|passage=They had found the world's first '''extremophiles''' – organisms that could live in water that had previously been assumed to be much too hot or acid or choked with sulphur to bear life.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020| title=Entangled Life|author=Merlin Sheldrake| page=95| passage=Lichens are ''''extremophiles'''', organisms able to live, from our point of view, in other worlds.}}

